{"pdfpcFormat":2,"disableMarkdown":false,"pages":[{"idx":0,"label":"1","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"We're Goose Chain. Our agent answers causal questions about ecological restoration, cites every claim, and in the judged run it never calls an LLM."},{"idx":1,"label":"1","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"Every question asks: what effect does X have on Y? The answer lives in a graph of 5,554 claims from 293 papers. About a third of questions have no evidence, and saying so is the right answer. We're scored on being right, calibrated, cited, and cheap."},{"idx":2,"label":"1","overlay":1,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"Every question asks: what effect does X have on Y? The answer lives in a graph of 5,554 claims from 293 papers. About a third of questions have no evidence, and saying so is the right answer. We're scored on being right, calibrated, cited, and cheap."},{"idx":3,"label":"2","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"So we profiled the graph first. 4,801 of 4,820 concept pairs rest on a single paper. 661 signs flip under a naive reading: decreased mortality is good news. And 1,093 findings are nulls, which are not decreases. So the job is finding the right edges and reading each one the way its sentence reads, with plain rules."},{"idx":4,"label":"2","overlay":1,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"So we profiled the graph first. 4,801 of 4,820 concept pairs rest on a single paper. 661 signs flip under a naive reading: decreased mortality is good news. And 1,093 findings are nulls, which are not decreases. So the job is finding the right edges and reading each one the way its sentence reads, with plain rules."},{"idx":5,"label":"2","overlay":2,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"So we profiled the graph first. 4,801 of 4,820 concept pairs rest on a single paper. 661 signs flip under a naive reading: decreased mortality is good news. And 1,093 findings are nulls, which are not decreases. So the job is finding the right edges and reading each one the way its sentence reads, with plain rules."},{"idx":6,"label":"2","overlay":3,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"So we profiled the graph first. 4,801 of 4,820 concept pairs rest on a single paper. 661 signs flip under a naive reading: decreased mortality is good news. And 1,093 findings are nulls, which are not decreases. So the job is finding the right edges and reading each one the way its sentence reads, with plain rules."},{"idx":7,"label":"3","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"The pipeline is four plain steps. Read the question. Link each side to a small offline taxonomy: 82 classes over about 6,000 labelled nodes. Interpret each edge as its sentence reads. Then one vote per study, two thirds to call a direction, graded, cited, and written from a template. Each stage is a frozen contract, so a new idea is one new file."},{"idx":8,"label":"3","overlay":1,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"The pipeline is four plain steps. Read the question. Link each side to a small offline taxonomy: 82 classes over about 6,000 labelled nodes. Interpret each edge as its sentence reads. Then one vote per study, two thirds to call a direction, graded, cited, and written from a template. Each stage is a frozen contract, so a new idea is one new file."},{"idx":9,"label":"4","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"We expected the LLM to do the linking. It lost. With the LLM linking, we scored 0.430 at 813 tokens a question. Plain node voting scored 0.549 at zero tokens. Embeddings linked about 40% wrong, so they only propose synonyms offline, for an audit to accept."},{"idx":10,"label":"4","overlay":1,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"We expected the LLM to do the linking. It lost. With the LLM linking, we scored 0.430 at 813 tokens a question. Plain node voting scored 0.549 at zero tokens. Embeddings linked about 40% wrong, so they only propose synonyms offline, for an audit to accept."},{"idx":11,"label":"4","overlay":2,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"We expected the LLM to do the linking. It lost. With the LLM linking, we scored 0.430 at 813 tokens a question. Plain node voting scored 0.549 at zero tokens. Embeddings linked about 40% wrong, so they only propose synonyms offline, for an audit to accept."},{"idx":12,"label":"5","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"Hand the engine the correct edges and it gets every direction right. End to end, with edges it finds itself, direction is 0.54. So retrieval is the bottleneck, and every gain came from finding better. Accuracy on our 267 dev questions climbed from 0.47 to 0.648, still at zero calls."},{"idx":13,"label":"5","overlay":1,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"Hand the engine the correct edges and it gets every direction right. End to end, with edges it finds itself, direction is 0.54. So retrieval is the bottleneck, and every gain came from finding better. Accuracy on our 267 dev questions climbed from 0.47 to 0.648, still at zero calls."},{"idx":14,"label":"6","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"Say you're a restoration manager. Mulch probably decreases invasive species, moderate certainty, two studies, every claim cited. The hedge word comes only from the evidence certainty. And when the graph is silent, as with herbicide and birds, we say so and show exactly what we searched."},{"idx":15,"label":"6","overlay":1,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"Say you're a restoration manager. Mulch probably decreases invasive species, moderate certainty, two studies, every claim cited. The hedge word comes only from the evidence certainty. And when the graph is silent, as with herbicide and birds, we say so and show exactly what we searched."},{"idx":16,"label":"7","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"Now the honest part. On dev we score 0.648. On our single holdout pass, 0.41. Retrieval shows why: it finds 0.44 of the right edges there, against 0.58 on dev. Our fitted confidence also missed on holdout, so we ship a flat 0.6 and publish both misses on a limits page."},{"idx":17,"label":"7","overlay":1,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"Now the honest part. On dev we score 0.648. On our single holdout pass, 0.41. Retrieval shows why: it finds 0.44 of the right edges there, against 0.58 on dev. Our fitted confidence also missed on holdout, so we ship a flat 0.6 and publish both misses on a limits page."},{"idx":18,"label":"7","overlay":2,"forcedOverlay":true,"hidden":false,"note":"Now the honest part. On dev we score 0.648. On our single holdout pass, 0.41. Retrieval shows why: it finds 0.44 of the right edges there, against 0.58 on dev. Our fitted confidence also missed on holdout, so we ship a flat 0.6 and publish both misses on a limits page."},{"idx":19,"label":"8","overlay":0,"forcedOverlay":false,"hidden":false,"note":"Zero runtime LLM calls. 500 questions in about two seconds, and it passes on ARM64 with the LLM unreachable. A restoration manager gets a cited answer, or a clear \"no studies, and here's what we searched\". Right edges, faithful reading, honest gaps. Thank you."}]}
